intact supports a B4-B5-B6 chow, and W5-W6-W7-W8 can form two chows if a tile is discarded. T6 is less critical for patterns like All Chows or Full Flush compared to maintaining sequences.\n\nReason: Discarding T6 preserves key sequences (B4-B5-B6 and W5-W6-W7) and avoids exposing tiles critical for potential melds. T6 is a middle terminal with lower strategic value in this context, and its discard minimizes the risk of others completing their hands.\n\nAnswer: Play T6"}
